$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound (N-2). Commercial 2-bromonaphthalene (11) (75.0 mg, 0.36 mmol),
compound 4 (150 mg, 0.35 mmol), and Na2CO3 (0.30 g, 2.83 mmol) were
dissolved in a mixture of THF (7 mL) and water (5 mL). After N2 gas was
bubbled through the mixture for 10 min, Pd(PPh3)4 (12 mg, 10 μmol) was
added, and bubbling was continued for 5 min. The reaction mixture was
refluxed under N2 overnight. After the mixture cooled to room
temperature, water (10 mL) was added, and the mixture was extracted with
CH2Cl2. The combined organic phases were evaporated after drying over
anhydrous MgSO4. Column chromatography on silica gel with a 2:3 (v/v)
mixture of pentane and CH2Cl2 gave the product as a light yellow solid
(146 mg, 0.34 mmol, 97%). mp 124-126 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, acetone-d6): δ
[ppm] = 8.13-8,07 (m, 1 H), 7.95-7.85 (m, 3H), 7.79 (dd, J = 8.6, 1.9 Hz,
1 H), 7.69-7.60 (m, 2H), 7.54-7.42 (m, 2 H), 7.14-7.05 (m, 4 H),
7.00-6.88 (m, 6 H), 3.80 (s, 6 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, acetone-d6): δ [ppm]
= 157.5, 149.6, 141.7, 139.0, 135.1, 133.5, 133.3, 129.4, 129.1, 128.7,
128.6, 127.9, 127.3, 126.7, 126.0, 125.3, 121.2, 115.9, 55.9. HRMS (ESI
TOF) m/z: [M]+ calcd for C30H25NO2 431.1880; found 431.1876. Anal. Calcd
for for C30H25NO2: C, 83.50; H, 5.84; N, 3.25. Found: C, 83.08; H, 5.94;
N, 3.23.
