$DATUM 14221-01-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Under nitrogen atmosphere, aryl boronic acid (5.2 mmol) was added to a
mixture of 2-chloro-6-methylpyrazine (514 mg, 4.0 mmol), Pd(PPh3)4(46 mg,
0.04 mmol), toluene (12.0 mL), and water (12.0 mL). The resulted solution
was heated to 95 °C for 10 min. Then, it was cooled down to room
temperature and potassium fluoride dihydrate (612 mg, 6.5 mmol) was added
in one portion. The resulted mixture heated at 95 °C until
2-chloro-6-methylpyrazine was consumed. The mixture was cooled down and
the phases were separated. The aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl
acetate (10 mL×2). The combined organic layer was washed with brine,
dried over sodium sulfate, and concentrated in vacuo. Column
chromatography of the residue on silica gel using petroleum ether/ethyl
acetate (20:1) as the eluent. The desired coupling product S3a-m. The
physical data of the new compounds were given vide infra.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Chiral Piperazines via Hydrogenation of Pyrazines Activated
by Alkyl Halides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
